4. DATABASE RIGHTS (Sui Generis)
══════════════════════════════════

The structured database — including the selection, arrangement, and
organization of catalog records, metadata, and cross-references — is
protected under the EU Database Directive (96/9/EC) and Dutch copyright
law (Databankenwet).

Database rights are currently held by:

    PlayPower Labs B.V.
    Amsterdam, The Netherlands

These rights are expected to be formally transferred to the Embassy of
the Free Mind (Bibliotheca Philosophica Hermetica) upon execution of a
transfer agreement. This file will be updated when that transfer is
complete.

The database is made available for non-commercial research and
educational use. Commercial use of substantial portions of the database
requires a separate license. Contact: derek@sourcelibrary.org


5. THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
═══════════════════════

Digitized page images are sourced from partner institutions (Internet
Archive, Bibliotheca Philosophica Hermetica, e-rara, Gallica, HathiTrust,
and others). These images are subject to the terms of their respective
holding institutions. Source Library does not claim copyright over
third-party digitizations.

Attribution to contributing institutions is provided on a per-book basis
within the application.
